# Find an object of a class and keep a TF frame on it while it is seen. If it is lost for longer
# than lost_timeout_s, another object of the class is chosen (reacquire) or the goal ends. It runs
# until it is cancelled or the object is lost. Served by /perception_orchestrator (the behavior
# track_object).

string class_name
# Its base category, also searched (as in StartDetection)
string category
# Which object of the class: nearest (to the camera) or first (the first one confirmed)
string selection
# The TF frame to publish. Empty: tracked_<class>
string frame_id
# How long to search for the object at the start. 0: no limit
float32 find_timeout_s
# How long it may be out of view before it is lost. 0: 2 s
float32 lost_timeout_s
# When the object is lost, track another object of the class instead of ending
bool reacquire
# The detection model (empty: the default of the system): omdet, grounding_dino, yolo,
# yolo_world, sam3, color_blobs (docs/MODELS.md); its options, YAML (e.g. "{threshold: 0.35}")
string model
string model_options
# The tracker (empty: the default): strongsort, bytetrack, botsort, ocsort, deepocsort
string tracker
---
# Why it ended: cancelled, not found, lost
string reason
# The tracker id of the last object tracked (empty if none was found)
string id
---
# SEARCHING, TRACKING or LOST
string state
string id
# The object, as the detection request sees it in the last image (has_position false if unknown)
TrackedObject object
